{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-ance-llama70b", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "5-2_10", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Yes, all babies cry, and it's normal for them to cry for about 1 to 3 hours a day. Some babies, however, cry much more than that, and this is known as colic. Colicky babies may cry continuously for 2 to 3 hours at a time for no apparent reason, and their crying spells usually happen around the same time every day, often in the evening. The good news is that most babies outgrow this excessive crying by around 3 months of age. So, it's not uncommon for babies to cry, but it's great that you're preparing yourself for this. Just remember that you're not alone, and there are many resources available to help you and your baby. By being with your crying baby and comforting them, you're teaching them that they're not alone and that you'll stick by them through thick and thin. This is an important part of their development and will help them feel secure and loved. So, don't worry", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0026-56-09659:2": 8.197722434997559, "clueweb22-en0016-36-07010:1": 7.996700763702393, "clueweb22-en0001-28-08060:7": 7.634530544281006, "clueweb22-en0029-92-05890:2": 7.623401165008545, "clueweb22-en0026-56-09659:1": 7.620340347290039}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I am a woman."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0026-56-09659:2": 8.197722434997559, "clueweb22-en0016-36-07010:1": 7.996700763702393, "clueweb22-en0001-28-08060:7": 7.634530544281006, "clueweb22-en0029-92-05890:2": 7.623401165008545, "clueweb22-en0026-56-09659:1": 7.620340347290039, "clueweb22-en0041-37-00654:0": 7.492656707763672, "clueweb22-en0044-10-12878:10": 7.457433223724365, "clueweb22-en0042-11-04140:3": 7.239043235778809, "clueweb22-en0015-34-03797:3": 7.231536865234375, "clueweb22-en0016-36-07010:0": 7.035653591156006, "clueweb22-en0029-12-11547:4": 7.013322830200195, "clueweb22-en0002-73-00932:5": 6.994697570800781, "clueweb22-en0000-85-09747:5": 6.9196105