{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-ance-llama70b", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "8-1_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "Meetings can be a significant distraction, especially if you're in the middle of a hyperfocus session. One strategy to minimize the impact of meetings is to schedule them at specific times, like you mentioned, and plan your focused work sessions around them. You can also try to prepare for meetings in advance by reviewing the agenda, thinking about the topics you want to discuss, and even practicing your responses. This way, you can feel more in control and focused during the meeting. Additionally, you can use the time between meetings to your advantage by working on tasks that require less concentration, like responding to emails or making phone calls. This can help you stay productive and make the most of your time. Another approach is to use the \"Flowtime\" technique, which I mentioned earlier, to work on tasks during meetings. This way, you can still be present and engaged during the meeting, but also make progress on your tasks. It's all about finding a balance between being present and being productive.", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0038-88-03812:10": 3.369783878326416, "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:2": 2.6736550331115723, "clueweb22-en0006-62-03234:3": 2.565673828125, "clueweb22-en0030-54-15087:4": 2.4959607124328613, "clueweb22-en0013-60-10409:8": 2.451801061630249}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I work in an office.", "I have a sedentary lifestyle."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0038-88-03812:10": 3.369783878326416, "clueweb22-en0025-75-16053:2": 2.6736550331115723, "clueweb22-en0006-62-03234:3": 2.565673828125, "clueweb22-en0030-54-15087:4": 2.4959607124328613, "clueweb22-en0013-60-10409:8": 2.451801061630249, "clueweb22-en0041-12-03522:7": 2.3277125358581543, "clueweb22-en0022-36-14427:15": 2.314992904663086, "clueweb22-en0038-88-03812:9": 2.295017957687378, "clueweb22-en0033-66-16401:4": 2.260465383529663, "clueweb