{"metadata": {"team_id": "Organizers", "run_id": "orga-ance-llama70b", "run_type": "automatic"}, "turn_id": "9-2_8", "responses": [{"rank": 1, "text": "To use the chain breaker, you need to place the tool on the rivet where you plan to break the chain, and line the driving pin of the chain tool up with the rivet in a straight line. Then, force the rivet out to break the chain. To open your chain, you can use the chain breaker to push any pin with the chain tool, but don\u2019t push it all the way out or it will be really hard to get in again. Push it so that it will stay in the outer plate; to release it, twist the chain slightly. It should come off. Alternatively, you can use bolt cutters to break the chain. To do this, mark where you want to make the break on the chain, then open the blades and position the cutters over the mark. Close the blades and apply force until the chain has been broken. Make sure you\u2019re using a firm grip when closing the blades. If your grip is too loose, the blades may slip", "citations": {"clueweb22-en0031-00-17726:10": 6.18006706237793, "clueweb22-en0031-00-17726:3": 5.899322509765625, "clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:2": 5.4555840492248535, "clueweb22-en0031-00-17726:9": 5.331593036651611, "clueweb22-en0007-76-12829:5": 5.240730285644531}, "ptkb_provenance": ["I sometimes get overwhelmed by too many technical choices.", "I'm a casual bike rider.", "I have a small garage that I use as workshop space at home.", "I am not really handy with DIY."]}], "references": {"clueweb22-en0031-00-17726:10": 6.18006706237793, "clueweb22-en0031-00-17726:3": 5.899322509765625, "clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:2": 5.4555840492248535, "clueweb22-en0031-00-17726:9": 5.331593036651611, "clueweb22-en0007-76-12829:5": 5.240730285644531, "clueweb22-en0019-70-04653:14": 5.180112838745117, "clueweb22-en0007-76-12829:6": 5.107097625732422, "clueweb22-en0027-35-00252:1": 4.95928430557251, "clueweb22-en0007-76-12829:3": 4.955161094665527, "clueweb22-en0031-00-17726:0": 4.